rocesso de design ADDR","otimização de design de software","melhoria da experiência do usuário","como usar ferramentas de inteligência artificial","o que é event storming"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","event storming","разработка сайтов электронной коммерции","процесс дизайна ADDR","оптимизация дизайна программного обеспечения","улучшение пользовательского опыта","как использовать ИИ Агенты","что такое event storming"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تصميم ADDR","بناء مواقع إلكترونية للتجارة الإلكترونية","عملية التصميم ADDR","تحسين تصميم البرمجيات","تحسين تجربة المستخدم","كيفية استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هو التصميم ADDR"]}},"owner":"cjjohansen","repo":"drone-web","repoPath":"cjjohansen/drone-web","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.942Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"event-storming","description":"Domain knowledge for Big Picture Event Storming following DDD conventions. Covers element types, color coding, pivotal event placement, layout rules, and bounded context identification. Use when the user asks about event storming, domain events, bounded contexts, DDD modeling, Big Picture EventStorming, pivotal events, or event storming workshop conventions.","bodyPreview":"# Big Picture Event Storming\n\nDomain knowledge for Big Picture EventStorming, following Alberto Brandolini''s methodology and [DDD-Crew conventions](https://ddd-crew.github.io/eventstorming-glossary-cheat-sheet/).\n\n## EventStorming Levels\n\n| Level | Goal | Elements Used |\n|-------|------|---------------|\n| **Big Picture** | Assess domain health, discover bounded contexts | Events, pivotal events, hotspots, actors, systems, opportunities |\n| **Process Modelling** | Assess process health, find bott","body":"# Big Picture Event Storming\n\nDomain knowledge for Big Picture EventStorming, following Alberto Brandolini''s methodology and [DDD-Crew conventions](https://ddd-crew.github.io/eventstorming-glossary-cheat-sheet/).\n\n## EventStorming Levels\n\n| Level | Goal | Elements Used |\n|-------|------|---------------|\n| **Big Picture** | Assess domain health, discover bounded contexts | Events, pivotal events, hotspots, actors, systems, opportunities |\n| **Process Modelling** | Assess process health, find bottlenecks | + Commands, policies, query models |\n| **Software Design** | Design clean event-driven software | + Constraints (formerly aggregates) |\n\nThis skill covers **Big Picture** only.\n\n## Big Picture Elements\n\n| Element | Official Color | Sticky Size | Notes |\n|---------|---------------|-------------|-------|\n| Domain Event | Orange | Standard | Past tense verbs. Core element of all EventStorming. |\n| Pivotal Event | Orange (marked) | Standard | Most significant events. Sit **between** subdomains as boundary splitters. |\n| Hotspot | Neon pink | Standard, slightly rotated | Conflicts, questions, risks, pain points. |\n| Actor/Agent | Yellow | Small | Person, team, department near related events. |\n| External System | Pink | Wide | Deployable IT systems (Excel, microservices, etc.). |\n| Opportunity | Green | Standard | Positive possibilities. Added after consistent timeline. |\n| Value | Red (negative) / Green (positive) | Small | Like value stream mapping. Added after timeline. |\n\n## Workshop Process (Big Picture)\n\n1. **Chaotic Exploration** — everyone writes domain events individually, places on timeline\n2. **Enforce the Timeline** — group discusses, removes duplicates, orders chronologically\n3. **Hotspots** — mark conflicts, questions, pain points with pink stickies\n4. **Add Concepts** — introduce actors, systems, opportunities, value as they emerge\n5. **Pivotal Events** — identify the few most significant events in the flow\n6. **Emerging Bounded Contexts** — draw boundaries around event clusters\n\n## Pivotal Events — Key Insight\n\nPivotal events act as **splitters between distinct phases** of the business flow (Brandolini, [Avanscoperta](https://www.avanscoperta.it/en/eventstorming/pivotal-events/)). They are NOT owned by either subdomain — they sit **at the boundary between two phases**.\n\n### Placement\n\n- Pivotal events go **between** subdomains, not inside any one subdomain\n- They mark where responsibility or business state changes significantly\n- \"An event at the very beginning or the very end is not a good candidate for a Pivotal Event; a splitter needs to be somewhere in the middle\" — Brandolini\n- In a draw.io diagram, the yellow bar spans the gap between two bounded context ellipses\n\n### Identification Heuristics ([Michael Plöd](https://www.michael-ploed.com/blog/finding-the-turning-points-pivotal-events-in-big-picture-eventstorming))\n\n- Events that **trigger significant downstream activity** (the \"So what?\" test)\n- Events representing **key business decisions** or policy enforcement\n- Events involving **hand-overs to external parties** (boundary crossings)\n- Events leading to **lasting state changes**\n- Events indicating **bottlenecks or failure points**\n- Events with **compliance/regulatory significance**\n- Events impacting **multiple stakeholders**\n- Events with **high business value realization** potential\n- \"A Pivotal Event probably sits on the boundary of a subdomain\" — Plöd\n\n### Speed beats precision\n\n- Initial pivotal events are **provisional** — expect them to change as the model emerges\n- Detection prioritizes **plausibility and balanced distribution** over perfection\n- Whatever notation is used should be **easily reversible**\n- Don''t expect to finish the workshop with the same pivotal events you started with\n\n### Examples\n\n- \"Contract Signed\" — before: negotiation phase; after: execution phase\n- \"Payment Received\" — before: ordering; after: fulfillment\n- \"Product Added to Catalog\" — before: back-office management; after: front-office discovery\n\n## Layout Rules\n\n### Single Row Per Subdomain\n\n- All events in a bounded context appear in a **single horizontal line**\n- **NO grids or matrices** (no 3x3, 4x2 arrangements)\n- Only exception: truly parallel event flows within a domain may use a second row\n- Even then, prefer putting one flow logically after another in a single line\n\n### Timeline Flow\n\n- Events flow **left to right** chronologically (paper roll represents time)\n- Within a bounded context, group events by phase with small gaps\n- Parallel streams go top to bottom on the paper roll\n\n### Vertical Stacking for Dependencies\n\n- If subdomain A publishes events consumed by subdomain B, place B **directly below** A\n- Spatial proximity communicates the relationship — no async arrows needed\n- Stacking full-width lanes implies true parallelism; only stack below the *trigger subdomain*\n- Center dependent subdomains below their trigger, not below the entire row\n\n### Visual Layout\n\nPivotal events sit **between** boundaries — they are the seam, not inside either context.\n\n```\n    ┌── ── CONTEXT A ── ──┐            ┌── ── CONTEXT B ── ──┐\n    │ [evt] [evt] [evt]   │ [PIVOTAL]  │ [evt] [evt] [evt]   │\n    └── ── ── ── ── ── ──┘    |||      └── ── ── ── ── ── ──┘\n                               |||\n               │ events (async)│\n               ▼               │\n    ┌── CONTEXT C ── ──┐       │       ┌── CONTEXT D ── ── ──┐\n    │ [evt] [evt]      │ [PIVOTAL]     │ [evt] [evt] [evt]   │\n    └── ── ── ── ── ──┘               └── ── ── ── ── ── ──┘\n```\n\n### Pivotal Events with Multiple Subscribers (Split Layout)\n\nA pivotal event that triggers reactions via policies may have **multiple subscribing subdomains** (n). The layout generalizes into two cases:\n\n**Even number of subscribers (n = 2, 4, 6...):**\n- Draw a **red hand-drawn line** at the pivotal event level\n- Stack **n/2** subscribing subdomains **above** the red line\n- Stack **n/2** subscribing subdomains **below** the red line\n- Primary/main flow subscribers go above; secondary below\n\n**Odd number of subscribers (n = 1, 3, 5...):**\n- Place **1** subscribing subdomain at the **same level** as the pivotal (continues the main line)\n- If n > 1: draw red lines **above and below** the center subdomain\n- Stack **(n-1)/2** subscribers above the upper red line\n- Stack **(n-1)/2** subscribers below the lower red line\n- When n = 1, no red line needed — simple sequential continuation\n\n```\nEVEN (4):        ODD (3):         ODD (1):\n  [A]              [A]\n  [B]            ═ red ═\n═ red ═            [B] ← center    [A] ← same lane\n  [C]            ═ red ═\n  [D]              [C]\n```\n\nThis visually communicates the fan-out — the pivotal causes reactions in all subscribing subdomains. When stacking multiple subscribers above or below a single red line, space them vertically with enough clearance for their ellipses.\n\n### Red Separator Lines\n\nRed hand-drawn lines are **local visual separators** at pivotal split points.\n\n- Draw at the pivotal event level, separating above from below subscribers\n- Extend across the subscribing subdomain area (not full canvas width)\n- For even splits: 1 red line. For odd splits (n ≥ 3): 2 red lines (above and below center)\n- Do NOT use arrows or connectors — the layout communicates causality\n- Reference: [Brandolini''s Big Picture layout](https://blog.avanscoperta.it/content/images/2021/04/image--6--1.png)\n\n### Bounded Context Boundaries\n\n- Draw hand-drawn ellipses (not rectangles) around event clusters\n- Dashed/striped borders work well\n- Boundaries are emergent — they come FROM the pivotal events, not imposed beforehand\n- Swimlane dividers (red lines) between non-sequential clusters improve readability\n\n## Naming Conventions\n\n- **Domain Events**: past tense verbs — \"Order Placed\", \"Payment Received\", \"Product Added to Catalog\"\n- **Actors**: role or department — \"Customer\", \"Warehouse Team\", \"Partner System\"\n- **Systems**: specific names — \"Inventory Service\", \"Payment Gateway\", \"Excel Spreadsheet\"\n- **Hotspots**: questions or concerns — \"Who maintains compatibility rules?\", \"Real-time vs cached?\"\n\n## Source\n\nBased on [EventStorming Glossary & Cheat Sheet](https://ddd-crew.github.io/eventstorming-glossary-cheat-sheet/) by DDD-Crew (Kenny Baas-Schwegler, Chris Richardson) and Alberto Brandolini''s EventStorming methodology.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T15:09:42.297Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Domain-Driven Design Agents requiring advanced event modeling and domain analysis capabilities using Alberto Brandolini''s methodology","zh":"适合需要使用Alberto Brandolini方法ology进行高级事件建模和领域分析的领域驱动设计代理","ja":"Alberto Brandoliniの方法ologyを使用した高度なイベントモデリングとドメイン分析を必要とするドメイン駆動設計エージェントに適しています","ko":"Alberto Brandolini의 방법ology를 사용하여 고급 이벤트 모델링 및 도메인 분석을 요구하는 도메인 주도 설계 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de Diseño Dirigido por Dominio que requieren modelado de eventos avanzado y capacidades de análisis de dominio utilizando la metodología de Alberto Brandolini","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de Conception basée sur le Domaine nécessitant un modelage d''événements avancé et des capacités d''analyse de domaine utilisant la méthodologie d''Alberto Brandolini","de":"Ideal für Domain-Driven-Design-Agents, die erweitertes Ereignismodellieren und Domänenanalysefunktionen unter Verwendung der Methodik von Alberto Brandolini benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Design Dirigido por Domínio que requerem modelagem de eventos avançada e capacidades de análise de domínio usando a metodologia de Alberto Brandolini","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Domain-Driven Design, требующих расширенного моделирования событий и возможностей анализа домена с использованием методологии Альберто Брандолини","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يستخدمون تصميمًا مدفوعًا بالمجال ويتطلبون نمذجة أحداث متقدمة وقدرات تحليل المجال باستخدام منهجية ألبرتو براندوليني"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to visualize complex domain events, identify bounded contexts, and assess domain health using Events, Pivotal Events, Hotspots, Actors, Systems, and Opportunities, following DDD-Crew conventions","zh":"赋予代理可视化复杂的领域事件、识别有界上下文并使用事件、关键事件、热点、参与者、系统和机会评估领域健康状况，遵循DDD-Crew约定","ja":"エージェントが複雑なドメインイベントを視覚化し、境界付きコンテキストを特定し、イベント、重要なイベント、ホットスポット、参加者、システム、機会を使用してドメインのヘルス状態を評価することを可能にし、DDD-Crewの約定に従う","ko":"에이전트가 복잡한 도메인 이벤트를 시각화하고 경계가 있는 컨텍스트를 식별하며 이벤트, 임계 이벤트, 핫스팟, 참여자, 시스템 및 기회를 사용하여 도메인의 건강 상태를 평가할 수 있도록 하며 DDD-Crew 규칙을 따름","es":"Habilita a los agentes a visualizar eventos de dominio complejos, identificar contextos acotados y evaluar la salud del dominio utilizando Events, Pivotal Events, Hotspots, Actors, Systems y Opportunities, siguiendo las convenciones de DDD-Crew","fr":"Permet aux agents de visualiser des événements de domaine complexes, d''identifier des contextes délimités et d''évaluer la santé du domaine en utilisant Events, Pivotal Events, Hotspots, Actors, Systems et Opportunities, en suivant les conventions de DDD-Crew","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, komplexe Domänenereignisse zu visualisieren, beschränkte Kontexte zu identifizieren und die Domänen-gesundheit unter Verwendung von Events, Pivotal Events, Hotspots, Actors, Systems und Opportunities zu bewerten, unter Befolgung der DDD-Crew-Konventionen","pt":"Habilite os agentes a visualizar eventos de domínio complexos, identificar contextos limitados e avaliar a saúde do domínio usando Eventos, Eventos Cruciais, Pontos Quentes, Atores, Sistemas e Oportunidades, seguindo as convenções da DDD-Crew","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью визуализировать сложные события домена, определять ограниченные контексты и оценивать здоровье домена с использованием Событий, Критических Событий, Горячих Точек, Актеров, Систем и Возможностей, следуя конвенциям DDD-Crew","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تجسير الأحداث المعقدة للمجال وتحديد السياقات المحكومة وتقييم صحة المجال باستخدام الأحداث والأحداث الحاسمة والمناطق الحارة والأفراد والأنظمة والفرص ، متبعًا اتفاقيات DDD-Crew"},"useCases":{"en":["Modeling business processes for ecommerce websites using Big Picture Event Storming","Identifying pivotal events and hotspots in domain-driven design","Assessing domain health and discovering bounded contexts for drone ecommerce applications"],"zh":["使用Big Picture Event Storming为电子商务网站建模业务流程","在领域驱动设计中识别关键事件和热点","评估无人机电子商务应用程序的领域健康状况并发现有界上下文"],"ja":["Big Picture Event Stormingを使用して電子商取引のWebサイトのビジネスプロセスをモデリングする","ドメイン駆動設計で重要なイベントとホットスポットを特定する","ドローン電子商取引アプリケーションのドメインのヘルス状態を評価し、境界付きコンテキストを発見する"],"ko":["Big Picture Event Storming을 사용하여 전자상거래 웹사이트의 비즈니스 프로세스를 모델링","도메인 주도 설계에서 임계 이벤트 및 핫스팟을 식별","드론 전자상거래 애플리케이션의 도메인 건강 상태를 평가하고 경계가 있는 컨텍스트를 발견"],"es":["Modelado de procesos comerciales para sitios web de comercio electrónico utilizando Big Picture Event Storming","Identificación de eventos cruciales y puntos críticos en el diseño dirigido por dominio","Evaluación de la salud del dominio y descubrimiento de contextos acotados para aplicaciones de comercio electrónico de drones"],"fr":["Modélisation de processus métier pour les sites web de commerce électronique en utilisant Big Picture Event Storming","Identification d''événements cruciaux et de points chauds dans la conception basée sur le domaine","Évaluation de la santé du domaine et découverte de contextes délimités pour les applications de commerce électronique de drones"],"de":["Modellieren von Geschäftsprozessen für E-Commerce-Websites unter Verwendung von Big Picture Event Storming","Identifizierung von wichtigen Ereignissen und Hotspots in der domänengetriebenen Konzeption","Bewertung der Domänen-gesundheit und Entdeckung von beschränkten Kontexten für Drohnen-E-Commerce-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Modelagem de processos de negócios para sites de ecommerce usando Big Picture Event Storming","Identificação de eventos cruciais e pontos quentes em design dirigido por domínio","Avaliação da saúde do domínio e descoberta de contextos limitados para aplicações de ecommerce de drones"],"ru":["Моделирование бизнес-процессов для сайтов электронной коммерции с использованием Big Picture Event Storming","Определение критических событий и горячих точек в Domain-Driven Design","Оценка здоровья домена и обнаружение ограниченных контекстов для приложений электронной коммерции беспилотников"],"ar":["نمذجة العمليات التجارية للمواقع الإلكترونية للتبادل التجاري باستخدام Big Picture Event Storming","تحديد الأحداث الحاسمة والمناطق الحارة في تصميم مدفوع بالمجال","تقييم صحة المجال واكتشاف السياقات المحكومة لتطبيقات التجارة الإلكترونية للطائرات بدون طيار"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires domain knowledge and understanding of DDD principles","Limited to event-storming methodology and DDD-Crew conventions"],"zh":["需要领域知识和对DDD原则的理解","仅限于事件风暴法和DDD-Crew约定"],"ja":["ドメインの知識とDDDの原則の理解が必要","イベントストーミング法とDDD-Crewの約定のみに限定"],"ko":["도메인 지식 및 DDD 원칙 이해 필요","이벤트 스토밍 방법 및 DDD-Crew 규칙에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento del dominio y comprensión de los principios de DDD","Limitado a la metodología de event-storming y las convenciones de DDD-Crew"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances du domaine et une compréhension des principes de DDD","Limité à la méthodologie d''event-storming et aux conventions de DDD-Crew"],"de":["Benötigt Domänenwissen und Verständnis der DDD-Prinzipien","Begrenzt auf die Event-Storming-Methodik und die DDD-Crew-Konventionen"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de domínio e compreensão dos princípios da DDD","Limitado à metodologia de event-storming e convenções da DDD-Crew"],"ru":["Требует знания домена и понимания принципов DDD","Ограничен методологией event-storming и конвенциями DDD-Crew"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة بالمجال وفهم المبادئ التوجيهية لتصميم مدفوع بالمجال","محدود بمنهجية عاصفة الأحداث وتوافق DDD-Crew"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"7c8575383f69532b5e06dbcbc1747f75ac8e0a4feab0e8935fe303292dcbcb4c","qualityScore":49}');
