:["Partage de ressources et de connaissances","Développement d''applications avec React et Node.js","Utilisation d''Apollo Client pour améliorer la collaboration","Intégration avec des outils de développement comme CLI","Amélioration de l''efficacité dans le développement de logiciels"],"de":["Austausch von Ressourcen und Wissen","Entwicklung von Anwendungen mit React und Node.js","Verwendung von Apollo Client zur Verbesserung der Zusammenarbeit","Integration mit Entwicklungstools wie CLI","Verbesserung der Effizienz in der Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["Compartilhamento de recursos físicos","Compartilhamento de conhecimento em desenvolvimento de sistemas","Utilização de website público para compartilhamento","Desenvolvimento de aplicação para incentivar o compartilhamento"],"ru":["Обмен физическими ресурсами","Обмен знаниями в разработке систем","Использование публичного веб-сайта для обмена","Разработка приложения для поощрения обмена"],"ar":["تبادل الموارد المادية","تبادل المعرفة في تطوير الأنظمة","استخدام موقع ويب عام للتبادل","تطوير تطبيق لتشجيع التبادل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Apollo Client安装","Apollo Client教程","共享应用开发","知识共享系统","React开发","Node.js开发","CLI命令","Agent功能"],"ja":["Apollo Clientのインストール","Apollo Clientのチュートリアル","共有アプリケーション開発","知識共有システム","React開発","Node.js開発","CLIコマンド","エージェント機能"],"ko":["Apollo Client 설치","Apollo Client 튜토리얼","공유 애플리케이션 개발","지식 공유 시스템","React 개발","Node.js 개발","CLI 명령","에이전트 기능"],"es":["cómo usar Apollo Client","qué es Apollo Client","alternativas a Apollo Client","Apollo Client vs GraphQL","instalación de Apollo Client","guía de configuración de Apollo Client","desarrollo de aplicaciones con Apollo Client"],"fr":["comment utiliser Apollo Client","qu''est-ce qu''Apollo Client","alternatives à Apollo Client","Apollo Client vs GraphQL","installation d''Apollo Client","guide de configuration d''Apollo Client","développement d''applications avec Apollo Client"],"de":["wie man Apollo Client verwendet","was ist Apollo Client","Alternativen zu Apollo Client","Apollo Client vs GraphQL","Installation von Apollo Client","Konfigurationsanleitung für Apollo Client","Entwicklung von Anwendungen mit Apollo Client"],"pt":["como usar Apollo Client","o que é Apollo Client","Apollo Client alternativa","Apollo Client vs GraphQL","instalar Apollo Client","guia de configuração do Apollo Client"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агент Apollo Client","что такое ИИ Агент Apollo Client","ИИ Агент Apollo Client альтернатива","ИИ Агент Apollo Client vs GraphQL","установить ИИ Агент Apollo Client","руководство по настройке ИИ Агента Apollo Client"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام Apollo Client","ما هو Apollo Client","بديل Apollo Client","Apollo Client مقابل GraphQL","تثبيت Apollo Client","دليل إعداد Apollo Client"]}},"owner":"simnova","repo":"sharethrift","repoPath":"simnova/sharethrift","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.706Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"apollo-client","description":">","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# Apollo Client 4.x Guide\n\nApollo Client is a comprehensive state management library for JavaScript that enables you to manage both local and remote data with GraphQL. Version 4.x brings improved caching, better TypeScript support, and React 19 compatibility.\n\n## Framework-Specific Setup Guides\n\nFor modern React frameworks with SSR support, use these specialized setup guides:\n\n- **[Next.js App Router Setup](references/setup-nextjs.md)** - For Next.js applications using the App Router with React","body":"# Apollo Client 4.x Guide\n\nApollo Client is a comprehensive state management library for JavaScript that enables you to manage both local and remote data with GraphQL. Version 4.x brings improved caching, better TypeScript support, and React 19 compatibility.\n\n## Framework-Specific Setup Guides\n\nFor modern React frameworks with SSR support, use these specialized setup guides:\n\n- **[Next.js App Router Setup](references/setup-nextjs.md)** - For Next.js applications using the App Router with React Server Components\n- **[React Router Framework Mode Setup](references/setup-react-router.md)** - For React Router 7 applications with streaming SSR\n- **[TanStack Start Setup](references/setup-tanstack-start.md)** - For TanStack Start applications with modern routing\n\nThese guides provide framework-specific integration packages and patterns optimized for SSR, streaming, and React Server Components.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Step 1: Install\n\n```bash\nnpm install @apollo/client graphql rxjs\n```\n\n### Step 1.5: Set up TypeScript Code Generation (optional but recommended)\n\nFor TypeScript type generation (recommended):\n\n```bash\nnpm install -D @graphql-codegen/cli @graphql-codegen/typescript @graphql-codegen/typescript-operations @graphql-codegen/typed-document-node\n```\n\n```typescript\n// codegen.ts\nimport { CodegenConfig } from \"@graphql-codegen/cli\";\n\nconst config: CodegenConfig = {\n  overwrite: true,\n  schema: \"<URL_OF_YOUR_GRAPHQL_API>\",\n  // This assumes that all your source files are in a top-level `src/` directory - you might need to adjust this to your file structure\n  documents: [\"src/**/*.{ts,tsx}\"],\n  // Don''t exit with non-zero status when there are no documents\n  ignoreNoDocuments: true,\n  generates: {\n    // Use a path that works the best for the structure of your application\n    \"./src/types/__generated__/graphql.ts\": {\n      plugins: [\"typescript\", \"typescript-operations\", \"typed-document-node\"],\n      config: {\n        avoidOptionals: {\n          // Use `null` for nullable fields instead of optionals\n          field: true,\n          // Allow nullable input fields to remain unspecified\n          inputValue: false,\n        },\n        // Use `unknown` instead of `any` for unconfigured scalars\n        defaultScalarType: \"unknown\",\n        // Apollo Client always includes `__typename` fields\n        nonOptionalTypename: true,\n        // Apollo Client doesn''t add the `__typename` field to root types so\n        // don''t generate a type for the `__typename` for root operation types.\n        skipTypeNameForRoot: true,\n      },\n    },\n  },\n};\n\nexport default config;\n```\n\nThe typed-document-node plugin might have a bundle size tradeoff but can prevent inconsistencies and is best suited for usage with LLMs, so it is recommended for most applications.\nSee the [GraphQL Code Generator documentation](https://www.apollographql.com/docs/react/development-testing/graphql-codegen#recommended-starter-configuration) for other recommended configuration patterns if required.\n\n### Step 2: Create Client\n\n```typescript\nimport { ApolloClient, InMemoryCache, HttpLink } from \"@apollo/client\";\nimport { SetContextLink } from \"@apollo/client/link/context\";\n\nconst httpLink = new HttpLink({\n  uri: \"https://your-graphql-endpoint.com/graphql\",\n});\n\n// Use SetContextLink for auth headers to update dynamically per request\nconst authLink = new SetContextLink(({ headers }) => {\n  const token = localStorage.getItem(\"token\");\n  return {\n    headers: {\n      ...headers,\n      authorization: token ? `Bearer ${token}` : \"\",\n    },\n  };\n});\n\nconst client = new ApolloClient({\n  link: authLink.concat(httpLink),\n  cache: new InMemoryCache(),\n});\n```\n\n### Step 3: Setup Provider\n\n```tsx\nimport { ApolloProvider } from \"@apollo/client\";\nimport App from \"./App\";\n\nfunction Root() {\n  return (\n    <ApolloProvider client={client}>\n      <App />\n    </ApolloProvider>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Step 4: Execute Query\n\n```tsx\nimport { gql } from \"@apollo/client\";\nimport { useQuery } from \"@apollo/client/react\";\n\nconst GET_USERS = gql`\n  query GetUsers {\n    users {\n      id\n      name\n      email\n    }\n  }\n`;\n\nfunction UserList() {\n  const { loading, error, data } = useQuery(GET_USERS);\n\n  if (loading) return <p>Loading...</p>;\n  if (error) return <p>Error: {error.message}</p>;\n\n  return (\n    <ul>\n      {data.users.map((user) => (\n        <li key={user.id}>{user.name}</li>\n      ))}\n    </ul>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Basic Query Usage\n\n### Using Variables\n\n```tsx\nconst GET_USER = gql`\n  query GetUser($id: ID!) {\n    user(id: $id) {\n      id\n      name\n      email\n    }\n  }\n`;\n\nfunction UserProfile({ userId }: { userId: string }) {\n  const { loading, error, data, dataState } = useQuery(GET_USER, {\n    variables: { id: userId },\n  });\n\n  if (loading) return <p>Loading...</p>;\n  if (error) return <p>Error: {error.message}</p>;\n\n  return <div>{data.user.name}</div>;\n}\n```\n\n> **Note for TypeScript users**: Use [`dataState`](https://www.apollographql.com/docs/react/data/typescript#type-narrowing-data-with-datastate) for more robust type safety and better type narrowing in Apollo Client 4.x.\n\n### TypeScript Integration\n\n```typescript\n// Define types for codegen or TypedDocumentNode\ninterface GetUserData {\n  user: {\n    id: string;\n    name: string;\n    email: string;\n  };\n}\n\ninterface GetUserVariables {\n  id: string;\n}\n\n// Types are inferred from TypedDocumentNode - never use manual generics\nconst GET_USER: TypedDocumentNode<GetUserData, GetUserVariables> = gql`\n  query GetUser($id: ID!) {\n    user(id: $id) {\n      id\n      name\n      email\n    }\n  }\n`;\n\nconst { data } = useQuery(GET_USER, {\n  variables: { id: userId },\n});\n\n// data.user is automatically typed from GET_USER\n```\n\n## Basic Mutation Usage\n\n```tsx\nimport { gql, TypedDocumentNode } from \"@apollo/client\";\nimport { useMutation } from \"@apollo/client/react\";\n\ninterface CreateUserMutation {\n  createUser: {\n    id: string;\n    name: string;\n    email: string;\n  };\n}\n\ninterface CreateUserMutationVariables {\n  input: {\n    name: string;\n    email: string;\n  };\n}\n\nconst CREATE_USER: TypedDocumentNode<\n  CreateUserMutation,\n  CreateUserMutationVariables\n> = gql`\n  mutation CreateUser($input: CreateUserInput!) {\n    createUser(input: $input) {\n      id\n      name\n      email\n    }\n  }\n`;\n\nfunction CreateUserForm() {\n  const [createUser, { loading, error }] = useMutation(CREATE_USER);\n\n  const handleSubmit = async (formData: FormData) => {\n    const { data } = await createUser({\n      variables: {\n        input: {\n          name: formData.get(\"name\") as string,\n          email: formData.get(\"email\") as string,\n        },\n      },\n    });\n    if (data) {\n      console.log(\"Created user:\", data.createUser);\n    }\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(e) => {\n        e.preventDefault();\n        handleSubmit(new FormData(e.currentTarget));\n      }}\n    >\n      <input name=\"name\" placeholder=\"Name\" />\n      <input name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Email\" />\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={loading}>\n        {loading ? \"Creating...\" : \"Create User\"}\n      </button>\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n    </form>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Client Configuration Options\n\n```typescript\nconst client = new ApolloClient({\n  // Required: The cache implementation\n  cache: new InMemoryCache({\n    typePolicies: {\n      Query: {\n        fields: {\n          // Field-level cache configuration\n        },\n      },\n    },\n  }),\n\n  // Network layer\n  link: new HttpLink({ uri: \"/graphql\" }),\n\n  // Avoid defaultOptions if possible as they break TypeScript expectations.\n  // Configure options per-query/mutation instead for better type safety.\n  // defaultOptions: {\n  //   watchQuery: { fetchPolicy: ''cache-and-network'' },\n  // },\n\n  // DevTools are enabled by default in development\n  // Only configure when enabling in production\n  devtools: {\n    enabled: true, // Only needed for production\n  },\n\n  // Custom name for this client instance\n  clientAwareness: {\n    name: \"web-client\",\n    version: \"1.0.0\",\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Reference Files\n\nDetailed documentation for specific topics:\n\n- [Queries](references/queries.md) - useQuery, useLazyQuery, polling, refetching\n- [Mutations](references/mutations.md) - useMutation, optimistic UI, cache updates\n- [Caching](references/caching.md) - InMemoryCache, typePolicies, cache manipulation\n- [State Management](references/state-management.md) - Reactive variables, local state\n- [Error Handling](references/error-handling.md) - Error policies, error links, retries\n- [Troubleshooting](references/troubleshooting.md) - Common issues and solutions\n\n## Key Rules\n\n### Query Best Practices\n\n- **Each page should generally only have one query, composed from colocated fragments.** Use `useFragment` or `useSuspenseFragment` in all non-page-components. Use `@defer` to allow slow fields below the fold to stream in later and avoid blocking the page load.\n- **Fragments are for colocation, not reuse.** Each fragment should describe exactly the data needs of a specific component, not be shared across components for common fields. See [Fragment Colocation](https://www.apollographql.com/docs/react/data/fragments#colocating-fragments).\n- Always handle `loading` and `error` states in UI when using non-suspenseful hooks (`useQuery`, `useLazyQuery`). When using Suspense hooks (`useSuspenseQuery`, `useBackgroundQuery`), React handles this through `<Suspense>` boundaries and error boundaries.\n- Use `fetchPolicy` to control cache behavior per query\n- Use the TypeScript type server to look up documentation for functions and options (Apollo Client has extensive docblocks)\n\n### Mutation Best Practices\n\n- **If the schema permits, mutation return values should return everything necessary to update the cache.** Neither manual updates nor refetching should be necessary.\n- If the mutation response is insufficient, carefully weigh manual cache manipulation vs refetching. Manual updates risk missing server logic. Consider optimistic updates with a granular refetch if needed.\n- Handle errors gracefully in the UI\n- Use `refetchQueries` sparingly (prefer letting the cache update automatically)\n\n### Caching Best Practices\n\n- Configure `keyFields` for types without `id` field\n- Disable normalization by setting `keyFields: false` for types that don''t include an identifier and are meant to group related fields under the parent\n- Use `typePolicies` for pagination and computed fields\n- Understand cache normalization to debug issues\n- **Enable [data masking](https://www.apollographql.com/docs/react/data/fragments#data-masking) for all new applications** - it prevents components from accessing fragment data they don''t own, enforcing proper data boundaries and preventing over-rendering\n\n### Performance\n\n- Avoid over-fetching with proper field selection\n- Configure appropriate `fetchPolicy` per use case\n- Use `@defer` for incremental delivery of deferred query parts, and `@stream` for streaming list fields (`@stream` available in Apollo Client 4.1+)\n- **Prefer Suspense hooks (`useSuspenseQuery`, `useBackgroundQuery`) in modern applications** for better loading state handling and code simplicity\n\n## Ground Rules\n\n- ALWAYS use Apollo Client 4.x patterns (not v3 or earlier)\n- ALWAYS wrap your app with `ApolloProvider`\n- ALWAYS handle loading and error states when using non-suspenseful hooks\n- PREFER Suspense hooks (`useSuspenseQuery`, `useBackgroundQuery`) in modern applications for better DX\n- NEVER store Apollo Client in React state (use module-level or context)\n- PREFER `cache-first` for read-heavy data, `network-only` for real-time data\n- USE TypeScript for better type safety with GraphQL\n- IMPLEMENT proper cache updates instead of refetching entire queries\n- ADVISE the human steering you to look into Apollo DevTools when collaboratively debugging Apollo Client issues\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T13:42:03.953Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for JavaScript Agents requiring advanced state management and GraphQL integration.","zh":"适用于需要高级状态管理和 GraphQL 集成的 JavaScript 代理。","ja":"JavaScript エージェントに高度な状態管理と GraphQL 統合が必要な場合に適しています。","ko":"고급 상태 관리 및 GraphQL 통합이 필요한 JavaScript 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de JavaScript que requieren una gestión de estado avanzada e integración con GraphQL.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents JavaScript nécessitant une gestion d''état avancée et une intégration GraphQL.","de":"Ideal für JavaScript-Agents, die eine erweiterte Zustandsverwaltung und GraphQL-Integration erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes JavaScript que requerem gerenciamento de estado avançado e integração do GraphQL.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов JavaScript, требующих расширенного управления состоянием и интеграции с GraphQL.","ar":"مثالي لعميل جافا سكريبت الذي يتطلب إدارة حالة متقدمة وتكامل GraphQL."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage local and remote data with improved caching and TypeScript support, leveraging GraphQL and React 19 compatibility for seamless integration.","zh":"赋予代理管理本地和远程数据的能力，具有改进的缓存和 TypeScript 支持，利用 GraphQL 和 React 19 兼容性实现无缝集成。","ja":"エージェントにローカルとリモートのデータを管理する能力を与え、キャッシュとTypeScriptのサポートを改善し、GraphQLとReact 19の互換性を利用してシームレスな統合を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 로컬 및 리모트 데이터를 관리할 수 있는 기능을 제공하며 캐싱과 TypeScript 지원을 개선하고 GraphQL 및 React 19 호환성을 활용하여 무중단 통합을 실현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar datos locales y remotos con una mejora de la caché y soporte de TypeScript, aprovechando GraphQL y la compatibilidad con React 19 para una integración sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les données locales et distantes avec une mise en cache améliorée et un support TypeScript, en exploitant GraphQL et la compatibilité React 19 pour une intégration transparente.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, lokale und remote Daten mit verbesserter Caching und TypeScript-Unterstützung zu verwalten, indem GraphQL und React 19-Kompatibilität für eine nahtlose Integration genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar dados locais e remotos com cache aprimorado e suporte ao TypeScript, aproveitando o GraphQL e a compatibilidade do React 19 para integração sem problemas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять локальными и удаленными данными с улучшенным кэшированием и поддержкой TypeScript, используя GraphQL и совместимость React 19 для бесшовной интеграции.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء إدارة البيانات المحلية والبعيدة مع ذاكرة مؤقتة محسنة ودعم TypeScript، مستفيدا من GraphQL ومتوافقية React 19 من أجل التكامل السلس."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing efficient data caching for React applications","Setting up Next.js App Router with Apollo Client for SSR support","Managing remote data with GraphQL queries and mutations"],"zh":["为 React 应用程序实施高效的数据缓存","使用 Apollo Client 设置 Next.js App Router 以支持 SSR","使用 GraphQL 查询和变更管理远程数据"],"ja":["React アプリケーション用の効率的なデータキャッシュを実装する","Apollo Client を使用して Next.js App Router を設定し、SSR をサポートする","GraphQL クエリとミューテーションを使用してリモートデータを管理する"],"ko":["React 애플리케이션을 위한 효율적인 데이터 캐싱 구현","Apollo Client를 사용하여 Next.js App Router 설정 및 SSR 지원","GraphQL 쿼리 및 변이를 사용한 리모트 데이터 관리"],"es":["Implementar una caché de datos eficiente para aplicaciones React","Configurar Next.js App Router con Apollo Client para soporte de SSR","Gestionar datos remotos con consultas y mutaciones GraphQL"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre un cache de données efficace pour les applications React","Configurer Next.js App Router avec Apollo Client pour le support SSR","Gérer les données distantes avec des requêtes et des mutations GraphQL"],"de":["Effizientes Daten-Caching für React-Anwendungen implementieren","Next.js App Router mit Apollo Client für SSR-Unterstützung einrichten","Remote-Daten mit GraphQL-Abfragen und -Mutationen verwalten"],"pt":["Implementação de cache de dados eficiente para aplicações React","Configuração do Next.js App Router com o Apollo Client para suporte ao SSR","Gerenciamento de dados remotos com consultas e mutações GraphQL"],"ru":["Реализация эффективного кэширования данных для приложений React","Настройка Next.js App Router с Apollo Client для поддержки SSR","Управление удаленными данными с помощью запросов и мутаций GraphQL"],"ar":["تنفيذ ذاكرة مؤقتة للبيانات بكفاءة لبرامج React","تكوين Next.js App Router مع Apollo Client لدعم SSR","إدارة البيانات البعيدة باستخدام استفسارات وعمليات GraphQL"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires JavaScript environment","Specifically designed for React frameworks with SSR support","Version 4.x compatibility required for latest features"],"zh":["需要 JavaScript 环境","专门为支持 SSR 的 React 框架设计","需要 4.x 版本兼容性以使用最新功能"],"ja":["JavaScript 環境が必要","SSR をサポートする React フレームワーク用に特別に設計されています","最新の機能を使用するには 4.x バージョンの互換性が必要"],"ko":["JavaScript 환경 필요","SSR을 지원하는 React 프레임워크를 위한 특별한 설계","최신 기능을 사용하려면 4.x 버전 호환성이 필요합니다"],"es":["Requiere un entorno de JavaScript","Diseñado específicamente para frameworks React con soporte de SSR","Se requiere la compatibilidad con la versión 4.x para las últimas características"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement JavaScript","Conçu spécifiquement pour les frameworks React avec un support SSR","La compatibilité avec la version 4.x est requise pour les dernières fonctionnalités"],"de":["Benötigt eine JavaScript-Umgebung","Speziell für React-Frameworks mit SSR-Unterstützung konzipiert","Version 4.x-Kompatibilität ist für die neuesten Funktionen erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer ambiente JavaScript","Projetado especificamente para estruturas React com suporte ao SSR","Compatibilidade com a versão 4.x necessária para os recursos mais recentes"],"ru":["Требуется среда JavaScript","Разработан специально для фреймворков React с поддержкой SSR","Требуется совместимость с версией 4.x для последних функций"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة جافا سكريبت","صمّم خصيصا لأطر العمل React التي تدعم SSR","يتطلب توافقا مع الإصدار 4.x للحصول على أحدث الميزات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"eed94d5d00ae06c79a59d1f1d97b9f93e4307763b3da59a37891999082dfc8a8","qualityScore":47}');
