craftランディングページのシステムデバッグをAIエージェントで行う","ko":"Minecraft 랜딩 페이지의 시스템 디버깅을 AI 에이전트로 수행합니다","es":"Nuestras herramientas de depuración sistemática ayudan a los desarrolladores de Minecraft a identificar y solucionar errores de manera eficiente","fr":"Nos outils de débogage systématique aident les développeurs de Minecraft à identifier et à résoudre les erreurs de manière efficace","de":"Unsere systematischen Debugging-Tools helfen Minecraft-Entwicklern, Fehler effizient zu identifizieren und zu beheben","pt":"Depuração sistemática para páginas de landing de Minecraft com React e Node.js","ru":"Системная отладка страниц приземления Minecraft с помощью ИИ Агентов и Python","ar":"فحص منهجي لألعاب ماين كرافت باستخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي واللغات البرمجية مثل CLI","en":"minecraft landing page(s)"},"definition":{"en":"minecraft landing page(s)"},"features":{"zh":["自动化调试过程","提高开发效率","支持多种Minecraft页面","集成React和Python支持","提供详细的调试报告"],"ja":["自動化されたデバッグプロセス","開発効率の向上","複数のMinecraftランディングページをサポート","ReactとPythonのサポートを提供","詳細なデバッグレポートを提供"],"ko":["자동화된 디버깅 프로세스","개발 효율성 향상","다수의 Minecraft 랜딩 페이지 지원","React 및 Python 지원 제공","詳細한 디버깅 보고서 제공"],"es":["Identificación de errores en tiempo de ejecución","Análisis de registros de depuración","Depuración paso a paso","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo de Minecraft","Soporte para múltiples plataformas"],"fr":["Identification des erreurs en temps d''exécution","Analyse des journaux de débogage","Débogage pas à pas","Intégration avec les outils de développement de Minecraft","Prise en charge de plusieurs plateformes"],"de":["Fehleridentifizierung in Echtzeit","Analyse von Debugging-Protokollen","Schritt-für-Schritt-Debugging","Integration mit Minecraft-Entwicklungstools","Unterstützung für mehrere Plattformen"],"pt":["Depuração sistemática com React","Otimização de páginas de landing com Node.js","Análise de código com Python","Integração com CLI","Suporte a múltiplos ambientes de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Системная отладка с помощью ИИ Агентов","Оптимизация страниц приземления с Python","Анализ кода с помощью React","Интеграция с CLI","Поддержка нескольких сред разработки"],"ar":["فحص منهجي بأدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تحسين صفحات الهبوط باللغة البرمجية Node.js","تحليل الكود باللغة البرمجية Python","دمج مع واجهة سطر الأوامر CLI","دعم بيئات متعددة للتنمية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用AI智能代理","Minecraft页面调试","系统化调试工具","AI智能代理alternative","Minecraft页面开发","AI智能代理安装","系统化调试教程"],"ja":["AIエージェントの使用方法","Minecraftランディングページのデバッグ","システムデバッグツール","AIエージェントのalternative","Minecraftランディングページの開発","AIエージェントのインストール","システムデバッグのチュートリアル"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 사용법","Minecraft 랜딩 페이지 디버깅","시스템 디버깅 도구","AI 에이전트 alternative","Minecraft 랜딩 페이지 개발","AI 에이전트 설치","시스템 디버깅 튜토리얼"],"es":["herramientas de depuración para Minecraft","cómo depurar errores en Minecraft","depuración sistemática en Minecraft","alternativas a los depuradores de Minecraft","guias de instalación de herramientas de depuración","configuración de herramientas de depuración para Minecraft"],"fr":["outils de débogage pour Minecraft","comment déboguer les erreurs dans Minecraft","débogage systématique dans Minecraft","alternatives aux débogueurs de Minecraft","guides d''installation des outils de débogage","configuration des outils de débogage pour Minecraft"],"de":["Debugging-Tools für Minecraft","wie man Fehler in Minecraft debuggt","systematisches Debugging in Minecraft","Alternativen zu Minecraft-Debuggern","Installationsanleitungen für Debugging-Tools","Konfiguration von Debugging-Tools für Minecraft"],"pt":["como usar ferramentas de depuração","o que é depuração sistemática","alternativas para depuração de código","depuração de código vs teste de unidade","instalação de ferramentas de depuração","guia de configuração de depuração"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агенты для отладки","что такое системная отладка","альтернативы для отладки кода","отладка кода vs юнит-тестирование","установка инструментов отладки","руководство по настройке отладки"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أدوات الفحص المنهجي","ما هو الفحص المنهجي","بديلات لفحص الكود","فحص الكود مقابل اختبار الوحدة","تثبيت أدوات الفحص","دليل إعداد الفحص"]}},"owner":"penne-0505","repo":"minecraft_landing_page","repoPath":"penne-0505/minecraft_landing_page","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.740Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes - four-phase framework (root cause investigation, pattern analysis, hypothesis testing, implementation) that ensures understanding before attempting solutions","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   **REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** Use superpowers:root-cause-tracing for backward tracing technique\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - **REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** Use superpowers:test-driven-development for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\n**This skill requires using:**\n- **root-cause-tracing** - REQUIRED when error is deep in call stack (see Phase 1, Step 5)\n- **test-driven-development** - REQUIRED for creating failing test case (see Phase 4, Step 1)\n\n**Complementary skills:**\n- **defense-in-depth** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **condition-based-waiting** - Replace arbitrary timeouts identified in Phase 2\n- **verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T14:05:28.468Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Agents needing rigorous issue resolution through systematic-debugging methodologies.","zh":"非常适合需要通过系统化调试方法进行严格问题解决的技术Agent。","ja":"体系的なデバッグ手法による厳格な問題解決を必要とするテクニカルAgentに最適です。","ko":"체계적인 디버깅 방법론을 통해 엄격한 이슈 해결이 필요한 기술 Agent에게 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Técnicos que necesitan una resolución exhaustiva de problemas a través de metodologías de depuración sistemática.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents techniques ayant besoin d''une résolution rigoureuse des problèmes par des méthodologies de débogage systématiques.","de":"Perfekt für technische Agenten, die eine strengere Problemlösung durch systematische Fehlersuche-Methoden benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Técnicos que necessitam de resolução rigorosa de problemas por meio de metodologias de depuração sistemática.","ru":"Идеально для технических агентов, которым необходима тщательная решений проблем через систематические методологии отладки.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الفني التي تحتاج إلى حل دقيق للمشكلات من خلال منهجيات تصحيح منهجية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify root causes of technical issues, ensuring that fixes are permanent and reliable, by adhering to the Iron Law of NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST, utilizing systematic debugging principles for test failures and bugs.","zh":"遵循‘没有根本原因调查就无需修复’的铁律，运用系统化调试原则处理测试失败和Bug，使Agent能够识别技术问题的根本原因，确保修复是永久且可靠的。","ja":"テスト失敗やバグに対して体系的なデバッグ原則を利用し、『根本原因の調査なしに修正なし』という鉄則を遵守することで、Agentが技術的問題の根本原因を特定し、修正が恒久的かつ信頼性の高いものとなることを保証します。","ko":"‘근본 원인 조사 없이는 수정 없음’이라는 철칙을 준수하고, 테스트 실패와 버그에 대해 체계적인 디버깅 원리를 활용하여 Agent가 기술적 이슈의 근본 원인을 식별하고, 수정이 영구적이고 신뢰할 수 있도록 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a identificar las causas raíz de los problemas técnicos, asegurando que las soluciones sean permanentes y confiables, al adherirse a la Ley de Hierro de NO SOLUCIONES SIN INVESTIGACIÓN DE CAUSA RAÍZ PRIMERO, utilizando principios de depuración sistemáticos para fallos de prueba y errores.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier les causes profondes des problèmes techniques, en garantissant que les correctifs soient permanents et fiables, en respectant la Loi de Fer de PAS DE CORRECTIONS SANS ENQUÊTE DE CAUSE PROFONDE D''ABORD, en utilisant des principes de débogage systématiques pour les défaillances de test et les bogues.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die Ursachen von technischen Problemen zu identifizieren, um sicherzustellen, dass Lösungen permanent und zuverlässig sind, indem sie dem Eisernen Gesetz von KEINE LÖSUNGEN OHNE URSACHENFORSCHUNG ZUERST folgen, unter Verwendung systematischer Fehlersuche-Prinzipien für Testfehler und Fehler.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar as causas raiz dos problemas técnicos, garantindo que as soluções sejam permanentes e confiáveis, seguindo a Lei de Ferro de NENHUMA SOLUÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DA CAUSA RAIZ EM PRIMEIRO LUGAR, utilizando princípios de depuração sistemática para falhas de teste e bugs.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выявлять коренные причины технических проблем, гарантируя, что исправления являются постоянными и надежными, следуя Железному Закону НИКАКИХ ИСПРАВЛЕНИЙ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА, используя системные принципы отладки для тестирования неудач и ошибок.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء تحديد الأسباب الجذرية للمشكلات الفنية، وضمان أن تكون الإصلاحات دائمة وموثوقة، من خلال اتباع قانون الحديد لا إصلاح بدون تحقيق السبب الجذري أولاً، باستخدام مبادئ تصحيح منهجي لفشل الاختبار والحشرات."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging complex test failures","Identifying root causes of recurring bugs","Implementing systematic debugging for technical issue resolution"],"zh":["调试复杂的测试失败","识别复现性Bug的根本原因","实施系统化调试以解决技术问题"],"ja":["複雑なテスト失敗のデバッグ","再発するバグの根本原因の特定","技術的問題解決のための体系的なデバッグの実装"],"ko":["복잡한 테스트 실패 디버깅","재발하는 버그의 근본 원인 식별","기술적 문제 해결을 위한 체계적인 디버깅 구현"],"es":["Depuración de fallos de prueba complejos","Identificación de causas raíz de errores recurrentes","Implementación de depuración sistemática para la resolución de problemas técnicos"],"fr":["Débogage de défaillances de test complexes","Identification des causes profondes des bogues récurrents","Mise en œuvre de débogage systématique pour la résolution de problèmes techniques"],"de":["Fehlersuche bei komplexen Testfehlern","Identifizierung von Ursachen für wiederkehrende Fehler","Implementierung systematischer Fehlersuche zur Lösung technischer Probleme"],"pt":["Depuração de falhas de teste complexas","Identificação das causas raiz de bugs recorrentes","Implementação de depuração sistemática para resolução de problemas técnicos"],"ru":["Отладка сложных неудач тестирования","Выявление коренных причин повторяющихся ошибок","Реализация системной отладки для решения технических проблем"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء الاختبار المعقدة","تحديد الأسباب الجذرية للشراب المتكرر","تنفيذ تصحيح منهجي لحل المشكلات الفنية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires strict adherence to the systematic debugging process","Violating the core principle may lead to inefficient fixes"],"zh":["需要严格遵守系统化调试流程","违反核心原则可能导致低效的修复"],"ja":["体系的なデバッグプロセスへの厳格な遵守が必要","核心原則に違反すると非効率な修正につながる可能性がある"],"ko":["체계적인 디버깅 프로세스를 엄격하게 준수해야 함","핵심 원칙을 위반하면 비효율적인 수정으로 이어질 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere una estricta adhesión al proceso de depuración sistemática","Violación del principio fundamental puede llevar a soluciones ineficientes"],"fr":["Nécessite une stricte adhésion au processus de débogage systématique","La violation du principe fondamental peut conduire à des correctifs inefficaces"],"de":["Erfordert eine strikte Einhaltung des systematischen Fehlersuche-Prozesses","Verletzung des Grundprinzips kann zu ineffizienten Lösungen führen"],"pt":["Exige adesão estrita ao processo de depuração sistemática","Violar o princípio fundamental pode levar a soluções ineficientes"],"ru":["Требует строгого соблюдения системного процесса отладки","Нарушение основополагающего принципа может привести к неэффективным исправлениям"],"ar":["يتطلب اتباع صارم للعملية المنهجية لتصحيح الأخطاء","خرق المبدأ الأساسي قد يؤدي إلى حلول غير فعالة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"07044c8e673c7d4d6894926ec4bbb3d20a5dfbf48260e14c5d4a63a9b57a5f0e","qualityScore":46}');
